nd funds one autonomous fixed-target raffle clone atomically.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:103:    /// @return raffle Address of the newly created and activated clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:128:    /// @notice Returns the immutable implementation targeted by every registered ERC-1167 clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:138:    /// @return registered True only for a successfully created canonical clone.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:143:    /// @return raffle Registered clone address, or the zero address for an unknown identifier.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:24:///      owners burn them for redemption or refund. Each raffle is a fixed, non-upgradeable ERC-1167 clone with no\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:28:contract Raffle is IRaffle, ERC721, ReentrancyGuard, IERC721Receiver, VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:152:    /// @dev Constructor state belongs to the implementation. Clones share these immutables but hold isolated storage.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:153:    /// @param quoteToken_ Canonical six-decimal USDC contract fixed for the implementation and every clone.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:154:    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper fixed for the implementation and all clones.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:588:    ///      Initialization supplies the prospective prize token because clone storage is not populated yet; runtime\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
