{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"_kritt_extractor_helper\": true,\n  \"stub\": false,\n  \"stub_explanation\": \"\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Grant a nonzero operator approval over the caller's tickets in this raffle, without a lifecycle or ticket-balance requirement. Ends with an approval-state write, event emission, and successful return.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:56 ERC-1167 runtime emitted by Clones.clone - delegates calldata to the fixed Raffle implementation, preserving msg.sender and using the clone's storage.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:105 ERC721.setApprovalForAll - receives ABI-decoded operator and approved=true through Raffle's inherited public handler, without a lifecycle restriction.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - returns msg.sender, binding the approval owner to the external caller.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:409 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - receives the caller as owner; the nonzero-owner check passes, and operator!=address(0) passes the operator check at line 413.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:416 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - stores true in _operatorApprovals[owner][operator].\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:417 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - emits ApprovalForAll(owner, operator, true); the handler returns successfully with no return value.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Persist operator approval in the raffle clone, emit ApprovalForAll with approved=true, and return successfully.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 416,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller-selected nonzero operator becomes the second mapping key, approved=true becomes the stored value, and msg.sender supplies the owner key. Both supplied arguments also reach the event unchanged. Self-approval and repeated approval follow this same route.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This writes collection-wide authorization used by subsequent ERC-721 transfer and approval checks for the caller's current and future tickets in this raffle. The caller cannot supply another owner. The call makes no operator callback or asset transfer, and it does not invoke Raffle._update.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Revoke or leave unset a nonzero operator's collection-wide approval for the caller, in any raffle lifecycle state. Ends with a false approval-state write, event emission, and successful return.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:56 ERC-1167 runtime emitted by Clones.clone - delegates calldata to the fixed Raffle implementation, preserving msg.sender and using the clone's storage.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:105 ERC721.setApprovalForAll - receives ABI-decoded operator and approved=false through Raffle's inherited public handler, without a lifecycle restriction.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - returns msg.sender, restricting the affected approval owner to the external caller.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:409 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - the caller passes the nonzero-owner check, and the supplied nonzero operator passes the check at line 413; prior approval is not required.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:416 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - stores false in _operatorApprovals[owner][operator].\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:417 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - emits ApprovalForAll(owner, operator, false); the handler returns successfully with no return value.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Persist approved=false for the caller/operator pair, emit ApprovalForAll, and return successfully.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 416,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The caller-selected nonzero operator identifies the mapping entry under msg.sender; approved=false is written unchanged and included in the event. Repeated revocation follows the same route and still emits the event.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This removes the collection-wide operator authorization used by later ERC-721 checks. It does not clear separate per-token approvals or affect other owners' operator settings. Revocation performs no external callback or asset transfer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"flow_summary\": \"Reject a zero operator for either approval value before changing approval state or emitting an event.\",\n      \"flow_trace\": [\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol:56 ERC-1167 runtime emitted by Clones.clone - delegates the call to the fixed Raffle implementation and propagates its eventual revert.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:105 ERC721.setApprovalForAll - receives ABI-decoded operator=address(0) and either approved value, then forwards the arguments to _setApprovalForAll.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Context.sol:17 Context._msgSender - supplies the actual external caller as owner.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:410 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - the real external caller passes the nonzero-owner check.\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:413 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - detects operator==address(0).\",\n        \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:414 ERC721._setApprovalForAll - reverts with ERC721InvalidOperator(operator), before the mapping write and ApprovalForAll event.\"\n      ],\n      \"flow_terminal_action\": \"Revert with ERC721InvalidOperator(address(0)); leave approval state unchanged and emit no approval event.\",\n      \"flow_file_path\": \"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol\",\n      \"flow_line\": 414,\n      \"flow_input_to_sink\": \"The externally supplied zero operator is passed unchanged into ERC721InvalidOperator. The approval boolean does not alter this rejection; both granting and revoking a zero operator revert.\",\n      \"flow_security_relevance\": \"This is the reachable address-validation failure protecting the operator-approval storage write. The separate owner-zero guard cannot be reached by the specified real external accounts or contracts because owner is derived from the unmodified msg.sender.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}
